{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Codebase-health audit run 2026-08-05/06. 73 candidate findings were verified by independent\nblue-team agents that never saw the discovery agents' output; 27 survived a validity floor of 0.75\nand an impact floor of 0.5. Nine were dropped on citation vetoes or outright refutation — including\ntwo fabricated citations produced by the audit's own discovery agents, which is why the\nverification pass is load-bearing and not ceremony.\n\nRemediations were proposed by two agents working blind to each other; 16 of 20 moves converged\nindependently. Four divergent items went to OSS research, which overturned both proposers twice.\n\nFull audit record: `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-06.md`.\nDurable playbook: `.joe-janitor/tools.md`.\n\nScope note: the bridge/reconciler command-surface redesign that this audit surfaced is tracked as\nits own epic, not here. The `doctor`/`fsck`/`validate` consolidation is tracked on existing epic\n`dabb-7d4b-f5bc-40e6`; only two cheap decoupled wins from it are carried here.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Code-review provenance is wired: `--ref`/`--source` reach `CodeReviewRequest`, and results\n      carry `source`/`verified_at_sha` like the four sibling producers\n- [x] [operator-attested] The snapshot-entry contract is enforced by CI rather than asserted by an ADR\n- [x] [operator-attested] An `LLM-Review` vote provably attaches to the tree that was reviewed\n- [x] [operator-attested] `docs/exit-codes.md` covers every dispatcher arm and every emitted code, and CI keeps it that way\n- [x] `bug_close_reason_ok` and the `_attestation.py` module are deleted\n- [x] ADR numbers uniquely identify a document, and a new collision cannot merge\n- [x] [operator-attested] Comment triage complete across all six subsystem shards, with each shard's `do_not_move` list\n      preserved as the protection record\n- [x] [operator-attested] No library read path can terminate its host process\n- [x] [operator-attested] The \"passed but unsigned ⇒ retryable\" rule is available to CLI and MCP from one implementation\n- [x] One terminal-state predicate decides whether a blocker is satisfied, everywhere\n- [x] Retired config files honour the deprecation registry's `behavior` field\n- [x] `validate --fix` no longer advertises a repair it does not perform\n- [x] [operator-attested] `docs/chatgpt-agent-guide.md` no longer directs agents to the wrong command"}},"env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786214452682118001,"uuid":"35163b79-4234-4f0d-989c-659214374924"}